  Vulnerability: There is limited systematic evidence of widespread government suppression of AI risk discourse specifically; most documented cases involve national security information controls or dual-use research concerns that apply broadly to emerging technologies, not AI safety research in particular — making this claim conflate legitimate information governance with targeted suppression.

