aiting for automated medical breakthroughs and labor-relief tools. When regulators choose to freeze iterative development out of abstract, hypothetical fears, they are actively choosing to let people suffer from diseases that decentralized trial-and-error could have cured years earlier. Who gave any institution the moral authority to trade real human lives today for speculative safety tomorrow? Unlocking human flourishing requires dismantling these top-down administrative barriers and unleashing the full velocity of permissionless innovation.",
